{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep this ordinance in its season, from year to year (מימים ימימה).</b> From year to year. And we find its like (1 Samuel 1:3): ״ועלה האיש ההוא מעירו מימים ימימה״, and it is written (Judges 21:19): ״הנה חג ה׳ בשילה מימים ימימה״, (ibid. v. 11): ״מימים ימימה תלכנה בנות ישראל לתנות לבת יפתח״." "<b>And Rabbenu Ḥananel, of blessed memory, wrote:</b> How many times the Torah warned about keeping (שמירה) the Pesach, but this verse comes only to inform that from this year onward you shall know the time of the season of the coming year, and it warned to keep it. And from here is a proof that they would fix it by calculation (עפ החשבון). End of his words." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> למועדה — there is a season (מועד) when a man lays tefillin and there is a season when he does not lay them; Sabbaths and Festivals are excluded, for they themselves are a sign and do not require a sign. מימים ימימה — by day and not by night; the nights are excluded, for they are not the time of tefillin. Another interpretation: מימים ימימה — from here, that a person must inspect his tefillin after twelve months. It is said here מימים ימימה and it is said elsewhere (Leviticus 25:29): ״ימים תהיה גאלתו״ — just as there, a year, so too here, a year."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:40.969229650Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}